# Line endings must not depend on who checked the repo out.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine gives the working copy CRLF, while a
# Linux build checkout produces LF. That makes the *bytes* of the inline
# <script> block in every page differ between environments — which is fine
# today, but silently breaks the moment the CSP moves from 'unsafe-inline'
# to a 'sha256-...' hash, because the hash would be computed over different
# bytes than the ones served.
#
# Normalising here makes the served bytes deterministic and is a prerequisite
# for that migration.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
